-- title:
--   Finite action on the ∞-chart, transitive over the floor (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of the Laurent series field $L((\mathsf q))$ over $L$ which is assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb Q$, where $H=$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) is the kernel of the unit-group reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ coming from $q\mid q^2M'$; thus $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images, along $\mathbb Q\to L$, of that function field. Let $A$ be a commutative ring with compatible algebra structures on $L$ and on $K$, and let $j\in K$ have image in $L((\mathsf q))$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function. Write $B=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L144), the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, and write $F$ for [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull (q ^ 2 * M')`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305), the latter being generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the expansions `qExpand ℚ d jq` for nonzero divisors $d$ of $q^2M'$ (equal, by a cited result, to the $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$ $q$-expansion field). Then there exist a type $G$ with a group structure, a finiteness structure and a multiplicative semiring action on $K$, such that: the $G$-action commutes with the $L$-scalars; every $g\in G$ fixes each $x\in K$ whose image lies in $F$, and conversely every $x\in K$ fixed by all of $G$ has image in $F$; every $g$ fixes each element of the image of $A$ in $K$, and fixes $j$; $B$ is stable under $G$; and for all prime ideals $y,y'$ of $B$ such that $b\in y\iff b\in y'$ for every $b\in B$ with image in $F$, there is $g\in G$ with $b\in y\iff b'\in y'$ whenever $b,b'\in B$ satisfy $(b':K)=g\cdot(b:K)$.
--
--   The group produced is the group of diamond operators realising $X_H(q^2M')$ as a covering of $X_0(q^2M')$ with the indicated fixed field, and the last clause is the classical transitivity of a finite group of automorphisms on the primes lying over a given prime of the invariant subring, transported to the $\infty$-chart $B$ of the two-chart integral model. It is the $q=3$ case, and is used in the regularity analysis of the fibre of the localisation of $B$ at a prime above a cusp.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_mulSemiringAction_chartAlgInf_isPrime_conj_of_forall_mem_floor_iff_xH_of_eq_three.lean

